  "answer": "This feature has been requested before, and PowerToys doesn't have it. In #21313 and #28596 the maintainers said they have no plans to build it. #42868 was closed as a duplicate of #21313. Several similar requests (#33581, #44783, #31856) were also closed as duplicates, so there is nothing new to file. You can add a +1 or your use case to #21313. Until then, you have three options. You can lock the PC (Win+L) or put it to sleep. On a desktop, you can unplug the keyboard. You can also disable the keyboard in Device Manager (Win+X > Device Manager > Keyboards > Disable), which is the workaround suggested in #44783. Third-party keyboard-lock tools also exist. Some users run a small AutoHotkey script, and #21313 mentions KeyboardCleanTool as one example."
 },
